the output of ...make.index() is a list, so matrix multiplication is not
defined.

I am not sure what you want to do, but I would check if the
'inla.posterior.sample.eval' function could help.
There is recent change in it, so that you would need the most recent
testing version of INLA (and R-4.2), and then check out the new vignette
about that function.

