you have to do this last step manually. for a new point 'j', then you'll
get

	\pi( \eta_j | y)

so then you need to integrate this into the likelihood, like

	\int  \pi(y_j | \eta_j ) \pi(\eta_j | y) d\eta_j

like by approximating it with a sum

