Hello INLA groups,

I was trying to fit an additive mixed model like gamm() <https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/mgcv/versions/1.8-40/topics/gamm> function using INLA for continuous gaussian longitudinal data, where each subject has a different number of measurements. Suppose the gamm model with 2nd degree spline model for covariate t_{ij} is given by

y_{ij}= \beta_1*covariates + f(t_{ij}) + b_{0i} + b_{1i}*time + \epsilon_{ij},
where
image.png
The model is fitted with INLA as follows;
inla.fit = inla(Y~ time * weight + I(time^2)+
                       f(Intercept_ID, model="iid") +
                       f(slope_id, time , model="iid") +
                       f(Spline_ID, model="z", Z=Z),
                     data=TT, family="gaussian",control.predictor=list(compute=TRUE),
                     control.family=list(hyper=list(prec = list(param = c(.001, 0.001)))),
                     control.compute = list(dic = TRUE, waic = TRUE, cpo = TRUE))
My interest is to construct simultaneous confidence intervals for the first derivatives of the spline (of this form click here <https://fromthebottomoftheheap.net/2017/03/21/simultaneous-intervals-for-derivatives-of-smooths/>), where the derivative is
image.png
For gam fitted object, ginla() <https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/mgcv/html/ginla.html> function from mgcv package was helpful, this function is not suitable for gamm() <https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/mgcv/versions/1.8-40/topics/gamm> model. How can I do this for INLA fit object,  Any help would be appreciated.

Regards
Tafere

