Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/8kFrjddyIyE/m/9AcFu19KAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Inla.posterior.sample sample from the joint posterior distribution, and rmarginal only from the marginals. Anything that relies on the joint properties (such as relative orderings) would need to use inla.posterior.sample.
Also not that boy sampling methods only sample the model parameters and predictor values; if you need response level samples you have to add that as an additional step yourself.

Finn

